 "brief": "Chiral effective field theory and nuclear forces — We review how nuclear forces emerge from low-energy QCD via chiral eﬀective ﬁeld theory. The presentation is accessible to the non-specialist.",
 "extended": "**Chiral effective field theory and nuclear forces**\n\n*R. Machleidta,∗, D. R. Entem b*\n\n93 pp, 36 sections.\n\n**Abstract.** We review how nuclear forces emerge from low-energy QCD via chiral eﬀective ﬁeld theory. The presentation is accessible to the non-specialist. At the same time, we also provide considerable detailed information (mostly in appendices) for the beneﬁt of researchers who wish to start working in this ﬁeld.\n\n**Outline.** 1 Introduction and historical perspective; 2.1 Symmetries of low-energy QCD; 2.1.1 Chiral symmetry; 2.1.2 Explicit symmetry breaking; 2.1.3 Spontaneous symmetry breaking; 2.2.1 Relativistic formulation; 2.2.2 Heavy baryon formalism; 2.3 Nucleon contact Lagrangians; 3 Nuclear forces from EFT: Overview; 3.1 Chiral perturbation theory and power count; 3.2 The hierarchy of nuclear forces; 4 Two-nucleon interactions; 4.1.1 One-pion exchange; 4.1 Pion-exchange contributions in ChPT; 4.1.2 Two-pion exchange; 4.1.3 Three-pion exchange; 4.2 Perturbative NN scattering in peripheral p; 4.3 NN contact terms",
